{
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "name": "Four New York City Ida high-water marks and FEMA map matches",
  "description": "A selected comparison of USGS-observed post-Ida marks and effective FEMA data returned at those points on November 23, 2026. The FEMA layer is a current snapshot. Panel effective date does not reconstruct the map at the storm date.",
  "source_coverage": {
    "event_date": "2021-09-01",
    "selection": "Purposive cases testing two Zone X points, a Zone AE point with an NGVD29 static BFE, and a Zone A point with no static BFE. These cases do not estimate flood frequency or map accuracy."
  },
  "method": "Submit each USGS-published longitude, latitude pair (EPSG:4326) to FEMA NFHL layers 28 and 3 using intersects. Retain published subtype and SFHA flag, and pick the NYC study (DFIRM_ID 360497) from the panel candidates. Translate the unavailable BFE sentinel to null and retain the source value. No vertical datum transformation was applied.",
